pdl5 (slot-5 follow-up to glue5 0071 c6 and 0074 c9): the dependent-launch pair in glue5's split hc kernels.
- glm_glue_hc.cuh: glm_hc::finish_split (tf_glm_hc_finish_split / _f32w_split) and glm_hcp::partial_split<M>
  (tf_glm_hc_partial8_o1/_o2/_o4/_o8) call pdl_wait() then pdl_trigger() at entry, in every thread, before any read
  of x or the partials, any store and any exit (partial_split's squares block returns early; finish_split's warp 0
  returns after Sinkhorn); one trigger a CTA. hcPre launches them with Set.pdl_hc as hc_partial8 and hc_finish.
pdl_sites.py: PASS with it, FAIL without it (the split kernels NO WAIT at hcPre's two launch sites). Exact by
construction: the same instructions on the same values; only the order against the wait moves.

